      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved test. The original has several understandability issues: unused imports, an unnecessarily complex helper using `AtomicInteger` just to capture a loop variable in a lambda, an unexplained loop bound, cryptic variable names (`data`, `enc`, `dec`), and a loop counter starting at 1 for no obvious reason.Now I'll compile-check the file.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused imports, replaces the `AtomicInteger`-based helper with an inline assertion using an effectively-final local variable, renames variables (`data`→`original`, `enc`→`encoded`, `dec`→`decoded`) for clarity, and introduces named constants `MAX_DATA_LENGTH` and `NUM_ITERATIONS` to make the loop's intent immediately obvious."
